FILE ASSEMBLY, VERIFICATION AND VALIDATION                        9040 1451   18
A. Trkov, IAEA                                                    9040 1451   19
                                                                  9040 1451   20
The ENDF-formatted data from EMPIRE calculation were merged       9040 1451   21
consistently with the resonance data, including resonance         9040 1451   22
covariance file (see description below). The nu-bar values and    9040 1451   23
delayed neutron data from the BROND-3 file [1] were added,        9040 1451   24
including the nu-bar covariance data.  Cross-covariances of       9040 1451   25
nu-bar with other materials were removed because they referred    9040 1451   26
to obsolete MAT numbers.                                          9040 1451   27
                                                                  9040 1451   28
The assembled file was checked according to the IAEA              9040 1451   29
verification procedure [2]. None of the checking codes reported   9040 1451   30
any significant errors. Comparison with experimental data         9040 1451   31
from EXFOR confirmed that the data are representative of the      9040 1451   32
database on which the evaluation is based. The ACE file for       9040 1451   33
Monte Carlo transport calculations was produced as a result of    9040 1451   34
the checking process. This was used for further validation on     9040 1451   35
benchmarks listed below. Detailed results are presented in a      9040 1451   36
separate report. The following benchmarks were considered:        9040 1451   37
                                                                  9040 1451   38
