 EVALUATION PROCEDURE                                             9040 1451  154
                                                                  9040 1451  155
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                9040 1451  156
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               9040 1451  157
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             9040 1451  158
                                                                  9040 1451  159
 Available experimental data were interpreted  using              9040 1451  160
 nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-2.19b33 by                    9040 1451  161
 M. Herman et al [He01, He02]. This code integrates               9040 1451  162
 into a single system a number of important modules               9040 1451  163
 and features, relevant for this evaluation:                      9040 1451  164
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 9040 1451  165
   coupled-channels (ECIS03 by J. Raynal)                         9040 1451  166
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    9040 1451  167
   HRTW width fluctuation correction                              9040 1451  168
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      9040 1451  169
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 9040 1451  170
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                9040 1451  171
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   9040 1451  172
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                9040 1451  173
   discrete transitions                                           9040 1451  174
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL-2 library [Ri03]              9040 1451  175
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                9040 1451  176
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               9040 1451  177
   and gamma strength functions  based on the RIPL-2              9040 1451  178
   library [Ri03]                                                 9040 1451  179
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              9040 1451  180
   EXFOR/CSISRS library                                           9040 1451  181
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A. Trkov)                    9040 1451  182
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 9040 1451  183
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                9040 1451  184
   PrePro codes by R. Cullen                                      9040 1451  185
 - Checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                        9040 1451  186
 - Support for NJOY                                               9040 1451  187
                                                                  9040 1451  188
 PARAMETERIZATIONS                                                9040 1451  189
                                                                  9040 1451  190
 Following models and parameters were used in the                 9040 1451  191
 current evaluation:                                              9040 1451  192
                                                                  9040 1451  193
 Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-2 level                 9040 1451  194
 file, based on the 1998 version of ENSDF.                        9040 1451  195
 Prompt fission neutron spectra and niu-bar                       9040 1451  196
 calculation include contributions from thorium                   9040 1451  197
 and actinium chain (see description of the method                9040 1451  198
 used in Maslov V.M. et al, Eur.Phys.J.A18(2003)93).              9040 1451  199
 Niu-bar calculation was renormalized to evaluation               9040 1451  200
 based on experimental data (see niu-bar section)                 9040 1451  201
 Prefission neutrons assumed anisotropic following                9040 1451  202
 (n,xn) angular distribution.                                     9040 1451  203
 EMPIRE-specific level densities                                  9040 1451  204
 Exciton model calculations with code PCROSS                      9040 1451  205
 Cluster emission in terms of the Iwamoto-Harada model            9040 1451  206
 Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1)           9040 1451  207
 Mean free path parameter in PCROSS energy dependent              9040 1451  208
 (it was increased around 14 +/- 3 MeV to reproduce               9040 1451  209
 energy dependence of n,2n cross section)                         9040 1451  210
 Width fluctuations calculated within HRTW  up to 1.95 MeV        9040 1451  211
 Exclusive spectra available up to emission loop #  3             9040 1451  212
 Shell corrections according to Myers-Swiatecki                   9040 1451  213
 Emission width of ejectile 0 from 233Th multiplied by   3.330    9040 1451  214
 Emission width of ejectile 2 from 233Th multiplied by   1.500    9040 1451  215
 Coupled Channels (ECIS) used for direct inelastic scattering     9040 1451  216
 Direct contributions to continuum were smoothed using            9040 1451  217
 gaussian function                                                9040 1451  218
 For all nuclei: advanced treatment of fission                    9040 1451  219
 E1 strength function set to MLO1                                 9040 1451  220
 GDR parameters from RIPL-2/Exp.data+Plujko systematics           9040 1451  221
