B) COVARIANCE MATRIX OF THE RESONANCE PARAMETERS (MF=32)          9040 1451  623
   Below 4 keV - L.C. Leal (ORNL) by using the SAMMY code         9040 1451  624
                                                                  9040 1451  625
   From 4 to 100 keV - P. Schillebeeckx, I. Sirakov (IRMM, INRNE) 9040 1451  626
                                                                  9040 1451  627
  The covariance matrix of the average resonance parameters in    9040 1451  628
the unresolved resonance region was deduced from the covariance   9040 1451  629
matrix of the experimental data and the sensitivity matrix or the 9040 1451  630
partial derivatives with respect to the adjusted parameters.      9040 1451  631
The covariance matrix of the experimental data was constructed by 9040 1451  632
assuming the following uncertainties:                             9040 1451  633
                                                                  9040 1451  634
total cross section:                                              9040 1451  635
  - correlated          : 1.0%                                    9040 1451  636
  - uncorrelated        : 0.5%                                    9040 1451  637
                                                                  9040 1451  638
capture cross section                                             9040 1451  639
  - correlated          : 1.5%                                    9040 1451  640
  - uncorrelated        : 1.5%                                    9040 1451  641
                                                                  9040 1451  642
The sensitivity matrix was deduced with RECENT around the final   9040 1451  643
average resonance parameters used to construct File 2.            9040 1451  644
The covariance and sensivitivy matrix were constructed at the     9040 1451  645
energy points of the cross section data in File 3.                9040 1451  646
                                                                  9040 1451  647
Since in the fitting procedure only the neutron strength functions9040 1451  648
Sl for l = 0, 1 and 2 and the radiation widths Gg,l for l = 0,1   9040 1451  649
were adjusted, only the partial derivatives with respect to these 9040 1451  650
parameters were considered. The resulting covariance matrix of the9040 1451  651
adjusted parameters is:                                           9040 1451  652
                                                                  9040 1451  653
     Parameter    Rel. Unc.             Correlation matrix        9040 1451  654
                                                                  9040 1451  655
  S0    8.78E-5     2.0%     1.00   -0.61    0.86   -0.54    0.73 9040 1451  656
  Gg,0  23.6 meV    4.2%             1.00   -0.64    0.69   -0.58 9040 1451  657
  S1    1.90E-4     4.1%                     1.00   -0.54    0.74 9040 1451  658
  Gg,1  22.7 meV    3.7%                             1.00   -0.86 9040 1451  659
  S2    1.27E-4     20.%                                     1.00 9040 1451  660
                                                                  9040 1451  661
This covariance matrix was used to create file 32.                9040 1451  662
To construct file 32 a very small relative uncertainty on the     9040 1451  663
level distance was introduced and it was assumed that the         9040 1451  664
relative covariance elements for the reduced neutron widths can be9040 1451  665
approximated by the relative covariance elements of the neutron   9040 1451  666
strength functions.                                               9040 1451  667
